# Hook files must be LF.
#
# This repo has core.autocrlf=true on Windows, which checks hooks out with CRLF.
# git then executes .husky/pre-commit through /bin/sh, where a trailing \r turns
# the script path into ".../pre-commit\r" and the hook dies with "not found" --
# silently, because git treats a missing hook as "no hook configured". That is
# the same silent-failure class as the bug this hook exists to catch, so the line
# endings are pinned rather than left to each developer's git config.
.husky/pre-commit text eol=lf
